Let $\pi:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta$ be a proper holomorphic family of complex algebraic manifolds over the unit disc $\Delta\subset\mathbb{C}$, smooth over the punctured disc $\Delta^{*}=\Delta\setminus\{0\}$, with smooth fibers $V_{s}=\pi^{-1}(s)$ for $s\neq 0$ polarized by a class giving rise (via cup product) to a non-degenerate bilinear form $Q$ on the primitive cohomology in degree $q$. Fix $s_{0}\in\Delta^{*}$ and let $E=H^{q}(V_{s_{0}},\mathbb{C})$. Let $T:E\to E$ be the Picard–Lefschetz (monodromy) transformation associated with a counterclockwise loop around $0$, and assume $T$ is unipotent, so that $N=\log T$ is a nilpotent endomorphism of $E$.

(a) Show that there exists a unique increasing filtration $W_{\bullet}$ of $E$ (the monodromy weight filtration centered at $q$) such that $N(W_{k})\subset W_{k-2}$ and $N^{k}:\mathrm{Gr}^{W}_{q+k}E\xrightarrow{\sim}\mathrm{Gr}^{W}_{q-k}E$ for every $k\geq 0$.

(b) Let $F^{\bullet}(s)$ denote the Hodge filtration on $H^{q}(V_{s},\mathbb{C})$, transported to $E$ via parallel transport in a chosen multivalued frame; define the limiting Hodge filtration $F^{\bullet}_{\infty}$ as the limit, as $s\to 0$, of the appropriately twisted filtration $e^{-\frac{\log s}{2\pi i}N}F^{\bullet}(s)$.

Prove that:
(i) $F^{\bullet}_{\infty}$ exists, is a holomorphic filtration on $E$, and varies holomorphically in $s$ in the twisted sense and extends across $s=0$;
(ii) the induced filtration of $F^{\bullet}_{\infty}$ on each graded piece $\mathrm{Gr}^{W}_{k}E$ defines a pure Hodge structure of weight $k$;
(iii) for each $k\geq 0$, the primitive part $P_{q+k}=\ker(N^{k+1}:\mathrm{Gr}^{W}_{q+k}E\to\mathrm{Gr}^{W}_{q-k-2}E)$ is polarized by the bilinear form $Q_{k}(u,v):=Q(u,N^{k}v)$;
(iv) $N$ maps $F^{p}_{\infty}$ into $F^{p-1}_{\infty}$ for every $p$.

